## G5. Good to know
43: - A session waits for work by itself. It never decides for you or edits `.handoff/`. `handoff brief` shows what it's told.
# the brief a set-up session gets when it starts (the SessionStart hook of step 1's settings), its lines on listening and its rules:
Listening: you don't run `handoff wait`. When your turn ends, a hook listens for reviewer and brings you what arrives.
Rules: never edit .handoff/ by hand. Never merge, push or deploy without the operator's decision. A claim is not an approval.
# and handoff brief, typed in that session, shows: handoff brief: you are reviewer in quick. You and implementer, reviewer-2 hand work to each other through handoff. The operator decides.

44: - A session keeps its role through a resume and `/clear`. A new Codex thread needs telling again. Giving a role to another session takes it from the first.
# a resume: the same id, a new process

$ echo '{"session_id":"s-rev","hook_event_name":"SessionStart","source":"resume"}' | env CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID=s-rev CLAUDE_PID=<pid> handoff hook brief
handoff brief: you are reviewer in quick. You and implementer, reviewer-2 hand work to each other through handoff. The operator decides.
# /clear in Claude Code: a new id, the same process

$ echo '{"session_id":"s-rev-2","hook_event_name":"SessionStart","source":"clear"}' | env CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID=s-rev-2 CLAUDE_PID=<pid> handoff hook brief
handoff brief: you are reviewer in quick. You and implementer, reviewer-2 hand work to each other through handoff. The operator decides.
# a new Codex thread, after one that had the role:

$ env CODEX_THREAD_ID=t-one handoff role reviewer-2
You are now reviewer-2 in quick.

$ env CODEX_THREAD_ID=t-two handoff role
handoff role: no role: when the operator gives this session one, run `handoff role <role>`
# exit 2
# giving the role to another session takes it from the first:

$ env CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID=s-other CLAUDE_PID=<pid> handoff role reviewer
You are now reviewer in quick. Another session had reviewer; it has no role now.

$ env CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID=s-rev-2 CLAUDE_PID=<pid> handoff role
handoff role: no role: when the operator gives this session one, run `handoff role <role>`
# exit 2

45: - The implementer works on a branch of its own and never merges or pushes without your decision.
commit your work on a branch of its own, not on main; you don't need to ask the operator first
