47: - Codex asks you to review the new hooks: choose **Trust all**. `handoff` runs outside Codex's sandbox, so its notifications reach you. Without hooks, a Codex session doesn't wait for work, so you tell it when there is some.
# what settings codex --global says of the hooks and the sandbox:
to review the new hooks: choose Trust all. Sessions already running get them
sandbox, so its notifications and pop-ups reach you; handoff decide is
prefix_rule(pattern=["handoff"], decision="allow", justification="handoff runs outside the sandbox so that it can notify the operator")
# a Codex thread with a role and no hooks, its brief's line on listening:
Listening: Don't run `handoff wait`: Codex checks on a running command about once a minute, each time with a whole model call, which uses up the operator's plan. Instead, end your turn. If work waits for you, the operator hears of it and tells you. If your session has no handoff hooks, offer to set them up for every project: `handoff settings codex --global` prints them and where they go. With the operator's OK, add them. They work once the operator starts this session again.

48: - While an agent owes a move, your Mac stays awake for up to two hours. If it sleeps, nothing is lost.
# the limit, from the source: 74:const AwakeWithin = 2 * time.Hour
